{"name":"Carafe","hex":"#5d473a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carafe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bottle, usually glass and with a flared lip, used for serving water, wine, or other beverages.","A glass pot with a spout for pouring, used both for serving coffee and as a receptacle during the brewing process."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carafe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carafe","blocks":[{"text":"A carafe is a glass container with a flared lip used for serving liquids, especially wine and coffee. Unlike the related decanter, carafes generally do not include stoppers. Coffee pots included in coffee makers are also referred to as carafes in American English."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carafe","wikidata":"Q1104430"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"carafe":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-carafe.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/af/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-carafe.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-carafe.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/af/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-carafe.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-carafe.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Brown ornaments on doors, Reflections, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Brown_ornaments_on_doors%2C_Reflections%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/500px-Brown_ornaments_on_doors%2C_Reflections%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brown_ornaments_on_doors,_Reflections,_Rostov-on-Don,_Russia.jpg","share":0.30125},{"title":"Vase with lamps, Brown and beige textures, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Vase_with_lamps%2C_Bro